WEBVTT

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.190
<i>Ready... 1, 2, 3, GO!</i>

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.030
<i>Love life! Very! Very! Happy!</i>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.820
<i>Friendship life! Bouncing, jumping!</i>

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.530
<i>Adventure life! Heart-pounding, OK?</i>

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.490
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.130
<i>Rushing out onto the road to</i>
<i>school with the blue sky behind us</i>

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.090
<i>I like that! I like this, too!</i>

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.590
<i>I'll take it all, all of it~</i>

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.470
<i>A girl who imagines love is all romance</i>

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.220
<i>If I can attack, I'll do it boldly</i>

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.850
<i>Let's find an original vision for the future</i>

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>Sometimes, we'll have a secret love advice time</i>

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.610
<i>Who do you like?</i>

00:00:52.820 --> 00:01:00.160
<i>You've got a green light for love now!</i>
<i>It's your chance to move forward!</i>

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:00.990
<i>So, let's just</i>

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.990
<i>Have a blast! Fall in love!</i>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>Our youth is non-stop!</i>

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.170
<i>Run! Aim for the future!</i>

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.790
<i>Everyone gather</i>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.670
<i>For a happy ending!</i>

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.210
<i>Will tomorrow be happy or sad?</i>
<i>Will we idle our time away?</i>

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.300
<i>We'll work hard!</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.590
<i>I want to keep dreaming forever!</i>

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.810
<i>Let's fly out into the</i>
<i>world with all our strength!</i>

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.690
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.400
What do you think, Cyan?

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.690
Hm? Um...

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.490
Oh, you mean there? What do you
think about this chord progression?

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.910
I see.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.040
They may have lost the battle of the bands,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.660
but they seem to be
heading in the right direction.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.580
Yes, that's true.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:56.960
It's going slowly, but they
seem to be growing closer.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.470
Well, why don't we call it a day?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.100
Let's practice our own parts at home
and put it together again tomorrow.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.100
That sounds good.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.180
Okay, pyuru!

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.690
Um—

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.480
After tomorrow's practice—

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.690
What is it, pyuru?

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.240
I-If you're interested...

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.910
Tickets...?

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.500
T-Tozen Naru Kurikiri Maboroshi no An...?

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.500
It's "Tsurezurenaru Ayatsuri Mugenan," Cyan!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.630
"Tsurezure"?

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:40.260
If you're interested, I thought
maybe we could all go together...

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.970
Aren't they a very popular band?

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.140
Of course I'm interested!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.730
I'm so excited that I can go
to a Tsurezure concert, pyuru!

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.770
Retoree, thank you, pyuru!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.700
I see, so she's at BRR?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.780
Yes, sir.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.000
Has Maple noticed?

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.250
No, it does not appear so.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.540
And?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.630
Well, Plasmagica was all right.
They don't hold a candle to Criticris—

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.050
I don't care about the band!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.340
I want to know how the girl with the guitar was.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.260
P-Please forgive me!

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:31.560
It's true that there seemed to be
something about the girl named Cyan.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.100
I see...

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.650
It seems I was right.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.690
Cyan, huh? I'm sure she
will end up here one day.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:48.490
I must have her lead the best band
in Sound World and stand at the top.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.450
So what should I do about Cyan?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.830
Let her swim along a little longer.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.210
The higher she raises her
music skill, the better it is for us.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.760
Yes, sir!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.850
I can see Tsurezure soon, pyuru!

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.970
Moa, you like them that much?

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.850
I'm a huge fan, pyuru!

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.360
As we enjoy their concert, we must also
look into the secret of their popularity.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:22.360
But they really are popular, aren't they?

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.990
What kind of music do they play?

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.320
Cyan! You really don't know Tsurezure?

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.910
Uh... N-No...

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:38.130
Cyan... Where you live is a mystery...
and you didn't know St. Midi Girls' Academy...

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:41.590
What have you been doing until now...?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.720
Now, let us apply ourselves to our
training before today's performance, as well.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:55.480
Because spreading music from the
Far East in Midi City is our training. Right?

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.600
Girls, that's the spirit.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.690
Master!

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.690
It must have been fate that allowed us to
meet a master from the Far East of our birth.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:11.780
To be able to study under someone as
virtuous as you—we are very grateful!

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:17.410
Even if you say so, you girls
are not so much younger than I.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.710
You should not depend on me so much.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.040
Master, you are too humble!

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:29.930
With your virtue and skill at the drum,
we would like you to teach us what music is.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.430
Oh my, I do admire your spirit!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.350
Now, let us go.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.060
Yes, Master!

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.150
It's finally time, pyuru!

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.900
♪ The journey has begun... ♪

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.410
Tsurezurenaru Ayatsuri Mugenan...

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:02.750
...has come to bring you the
sound of our home, the Far East.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.880
I am called "A"!

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.300
My name is "Un"!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:13.760
And this is our master—

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.430
Master Darudayu!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.150
It will bring me great pleasure...

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:32.950
...for you to thoroughly enjoy our sound tonight.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:43.210
♪ The dream fireworks blooming
in the never-ending sky ♪

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:50.420
♪ The steam whistle of the night train blows ♪

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.350
♪ My heart is expectant and uneasy ♪

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.850
♪ In the dry night ♪

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.520
♪ I feel like something is about to happen ♪

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.520
♪ And I take a step in response ♪

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.150
♪ The faraway sky, the Milky Way ♪

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.400
♪ Shines with thousands of wishes ♪

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.820
♪ Idle thoughts constantly
changing into the night ♪

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:21.870
♪ The journey begins ♪

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.000
♪ Bloom, dream fireworks, in the blinking sky ♪

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.090
♪ On our journey, even when we find one path ♪

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.090
♪ Cherry blossoms of choices swirl around us ♪

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.050
♪ Like a bewitching and
maddening kaleidoscope ♪

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.260
♪ Bloom, dream fireworks,
in the sky of our destination ♪

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.930
♪ Journeys are partings with
once in a lifetime encounters ♪

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.060
- This is true ability...!
- ♪ Encounters on our path ♪

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:47.230
- Gap <i>moe</i>!
- ♪ Like a turning kaleidoscope ♪

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.700
It's not only their playing that is amazing.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:08:00.040
Their originality that
charms the audience is, too!

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.040
Master, what did you
think of today's performance?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.290
I feel the audience seemed to like us...

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.760
Master? What did you think?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.100
You girls still have far to go.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.940
You cannot just think that
it's fine as long as they like us!

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.560
What?!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:32.980
Was not today the first time
we performed here in Shibu Valley?

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:33.940
Yes, Master.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:39.740
In other words, the audience
merely found Far Eastern music curious.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:46.660
You are still inexperienced if you
mistake that for our own abilities.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.040
How could we make such a mistake?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.550
We have not trained nearly enough.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:56.340
You must be diligent every day to
walk the path of the performing arts.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.050
Work hard!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.890
Yes, Master!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.760
As long as you understand.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:07.810
Now, since we came all the way to
the town of young people, Shibu Valley...

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.190
...why don't we enjoy ourselves a little?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.230
That's what we were waiting to hear!

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.870
It's so yummy!

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:25.500
Tsurezure really has a lot of spirit, huh?

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:32.380
Yes. Their costumes, performance, songs—
they were all overflowing with originality.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.090
Moa?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.220
They were amazing, pyuru.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:44.010
You were so moved that everything's just
going in one ear and out the other, isn't it?

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:45.060
Pyuru...

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:49.690
You can't think of it from the point of
view of a fan. Those girls are our rivals!

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:53.570
Retoree's right. It's no time to be moved.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:58.030
We must also aim for the same stage as them.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.910
Is their originality what
makes them so appealing?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.330
That might be true.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.290
But don't you think that
Darudayu's <i>daruma</i> doll is against the rul—

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.710
Chuchu, what's wrong?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.720
So this is that "pancake" people
have been speaking of these days?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:25.970
It looks like no more
than a large <i>dorayaki</i> to me.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.770
But it looks delicious, doesn't it?

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:29.890
What should we do, pyuru?

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.730
Retoree! What are you planning—?

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.990
I...

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.330
Don't tell me she's declaring them rivals?!

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:47.830
It's still too soon for that!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.160
Stop, pyuru!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:54.420
I... I...

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.800
I'm a huge fan!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.050
Wha...

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.880
I am so very happy to hear that.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:06.300
Yes, I always support you!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.140
U-Um, pyuru!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.310
Yes?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.390
Moa...?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.440
Huh?

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:13.900
What?

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.440
Your lyrics based on your
thoughts of the Far East...

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.240
They touched me a lot, pyuru.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:24.030
Are you far from your home, as well?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:37.420
Your hometown is something carved in
your heart, no matter how far or where it is.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.090
By the way, who are you girls?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.180
That girl is...

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.770
Originality, huh...?

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.570
I guess we have to start with how we look.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:03.650
How we look?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.360
What do you mean?

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.240
I mean, we should <i>wear</i> our originality.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:12.330
Well, to put it simply, we need battle armor.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:21.670
What do you think?

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.550
It might be a little too bold...?

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:28.510
How is it, pyuru?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.310
Too clichéd, I think.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.310
That doesn't go with our songs, pyuru.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.690
That's not quite right.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.070
Aren't we getting further and
further from what we're looking for?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.580
Um...

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.370
We're not making any progress...

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.840
Which one do you all think works best?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.720
Oh, we weren't looking.
What are you talking about?

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.720
About our performance outfits.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:09.140
H-How should I know?!

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:14.810
For me, even if you were clad in rags,
my Ryukenden would stay pure. Hence—

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.640
It is proof you are ignorant
people who go against god

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.850
if your hearts are wicked enough
to be tempted by costumes like that.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.320
If you have reached the divine realm of god,
even if you were not wearing a thread of clothes,

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:26.110
you would be able to reach
the hearts of the audience!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.700
What are you guys doing?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:30.910
You're so noisy.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.580
Rom! Perfect timing.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:36.200
Can you tell us your opinion about something?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:40.290
What is it? I'm tired today for real.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.420
Curry for me, too.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.420
Okay.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:47.590
We wanted to try showcasing
more of our originality.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.470
Which outfit do you think fits us best?

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:57.140
Aren't you guys misunderstanding something?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.140
Huh?

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.770
Clothes don't determine
whether a band is good or bad.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.400
All we can do is fight for
real with our music laid bare.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:11.360
Yes, but yesterday, we went to the concert
of a band that became popular recently.

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:15.950
And then we thought, we need
originality to be popular after all.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.910
It's not just about being popular!

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.590
I've gotta get up early tomorrow...

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.970
Hey, Rom! You going home already?

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:34.800
Sorry. I said too much...

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.810
Sorry, I might've gone too
far with my own preferences...

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.900
No, I think I also got carried away.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:53.030
Can I change now, meow...?

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:16.470
Hey. Long time no see, Rom.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:21.430
Is it all right for you to be here? If anyone
sees a super famous guy like you here,

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.190
there'll be an uproar.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.690
I didn't get a chance to
thank you for the other day.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.240
Thanks for making me
shine on stage the other day!

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.660
You haven't changed. I still can't like you.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:45.460
I'm waiting for you.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:49.130
Hurry up and climb to my stage.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.960
You bastard!

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:03.770
Damn. I guess you haven't gotten soft.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.230
You—

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:13.150
Hey, Rom. Wait up!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.820
Those guys...

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.160
See ya, Rom!

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.080
Huh? Who was that? Someone you know?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.040
Not really. Anyway, what're you guys doing?

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:33.050
We were thinking of getting some ramen.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.300
Didn't you just have curry at the café?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.970
Idiot! Curry is a drink!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.810
Ramen is the Legend of
the Favorite Plate. Hence—

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:46.890
The matter in question is also carved
in the book of the Dark Apocalypse.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.400
It is not a prank of the rodent.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.570
I guess I have no choice!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:59.200
Let's go, guys! This guy with a
full-time job will treat you, for real.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:05.500
That's our Rom! Wait up! Hey!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:12.250
I think what Rom said makes sense after all.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.220
I agree. I don't think we
should start with appearances.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.720
We should win with our musicianship.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.470
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:26.060
Tsurezure knows a lot of ways to
present themselves when they perform,

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.400
and outwardly, they look very original,

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.690
but most of all,
it's their music, don't you think?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.530
I think they're the only
ones who can sing their songs.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.280
Yes, that's true.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:40.030
The Far East sound...

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:45.790
They're convincing because they're
singing with love for their hometown, pyuru.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.790
Their lyrics were close to my heart, too, pyuru!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.670
Oh, right. There's something
important I forgot to tell you.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:52.670
Huh?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:57.510
We haven't written a new song
since Cyan joined us, right?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.340
Yeah, that's true.

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.600
Do you want to write a new song?

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.850
A new song...? Wow!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.060
That sounds good. I'm for it!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.020
Yeah, I'm all for it, pyuru!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:16.070
Then, let's all come up with
some ideas before the next practice.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:26.660
I'm so dumb! How could
I leave Mr. Berry in the studio?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.290
He's going to yell at me!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.290
Huh? President?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.500
What are you doing here at this time of night?

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.130
Oh, uh, it's just my usual patrolling.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:45.010
Cyan, are you doing individual practice?
Oh, that's so admirable!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.220
Oh, Cyan!

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.310
Yes?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:52.480
This might be an awkward question,
but during the battle of the bands,

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.360
did Ogasawara from the other band's
agency say anything to you?

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.360
No, not really. What do
you mean by "say anything"?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:06.370
Oh, if he didn't, then it's fine.
Well, good night, then.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.540
Hm? Good night!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:21.630
♪ A miracle hidden in the cursed black stardust ♪

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.630
Crow has arrived!

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.010
♪ Fragrant for eternity in the darkness ♪

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:30.220
♪ The forbidden devil's sigh ♪

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:32.480
Breath breaker, Aion!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:36.110
♪ He tames the angry lake of hell flame ♪

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:39.110
♪ Legend of Tongue Flame! ♪

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.570
Hence, Yaiba appears bearing
his legendary Ryukenden.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.030
♪ Grown men need to intake fatty oils ♪

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.530
♪ Shining justice ♪

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:50.620
♪ I am Rom! ♪

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.160
♪ Sing, you cattle ♪

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.420
♪ Be clad in crimson ♪

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:58.340
♪ Sing in harmony now ♪

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:02.170
♪ Tonkotsu ramen ♪

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:08.220
♪ Tonkotsu ramen! ♪

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:25.650
Mama...

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.290
Oh, it's from Mama, pyuru!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:34.160
Moa, are you doing well?

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.250
Are you eating properly?

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:40.090
I want to eat Mama's cooking, pyuru.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:47.760
I'm waiting anxiously for you to
finish your mission and come home soon.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:52.520
Until then, work hard and don't get sick.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.600
P.S.—I thought you might be having
a hard time with unfamiliar food,

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.900
so I sent your favorite
nagonago fassagua by regular post.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.940
Boil or fry or steam it before you eat it.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:08.110
Oh, you absolutely cannot eat it raw, though.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.530
Make sure you cook it first.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.870
With love, from Mama.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.750
Mama!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.750
Mama, I want to see you too, pyuru!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:27.680
But, I met music and
friends on this planet, pyuru.

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:33.140
Music makes me really happy,
and it's really fun, pyuru.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:38.100
My bandmates make me forget
about feeling lonely, pyuru.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.480
I don't want to leave them yet, pyuru.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:49.070
I want to go home,
but I don't want to go home, pyuru.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:02.790
<i>If you like it, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.670
<i>You can do it because you like it</i>

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:08.380
<i>The feeling that you like music</i>

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.760
<i>Can't be stopped by anyone</i>

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:20.190
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:22.400
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:25.940
<i>Running through my body</i>

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:28.490
<i>This electric thrill</i>

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:33.490
<i>Is this feeling curiosity?</i>

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:37.040
<i>Negativity is a decrescendo</i>

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:39.710
<i>Hope and expectations, a crescendo</i>

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:45.250
<i>Show off our passion and</i>
<i>get god to be our ally, too</i>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:50.760
<i>I wanna share with everyone and have a taste of</i>

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:54.470
<i>Big!! Rocking!! Heart-throbbing!! Happiness!!!!</i>

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:58.520
<i>If it's you, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:58.720 --> 00:23:01.520
<i>You can do it because it's you</i>

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:06.610
<i>Let's try performing these</i>
<i>dream-colored notes together</i>

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:09.820
<i>I want to tell you directly</i>

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:12.660
<i>A life-sized, "heart-sized" heart</i>

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:15.530
<i>In order for it to reach you...</i>

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:18.870
<i>I will sing with all I have</i>

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:21.620
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.580
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.590
Oh my! I feel trouble brewing for next week!

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.590
Don't tell me BRR is going under?

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:31.300
No, no.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:34.090
Is Angelica leaving the company to get married?

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:38.100
Th-That would be a problem! What should I do?

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:39.600
I don't know.
